  "text": "Drag a bridge section and release to place it. Escape cancels the gesture. Ground and deck clicks walk Pip; drag another object to work on it. Place the two near-bank posts and two center posts, then draw both side ropes to the center posts before stepping onto the first section. From there, connect the second section, place the far posts and extend the ropes. Keyboard and precise controls offer the same placements and turns.\n\nMara lowered the page. “I miss it. My work hours changed before the storm. I used to finish before the storytelling began. Now I wait for the last boat and help everyone ashore. By the time I could reach the garden, they would have gone home. This page has made more trips to the dock than to Grandma.”\n\nNow the footbridge was gone. Last night’s storm had left a gap between the banks. Pip could see the garden on the other side, but seeing it was not the same as reaching it. He checked the seed, then unfolded Grandma’s letter. She had written it before the storm.\n\nMy small boat can carry the seed, but it cannot carry Pip. Load the seed at the yellow launch. Steer around the rock to my blue landing. I will come to collect the seed and bring it to our planting spot. You may also carry the seed across the secured bridge.\n\n“Keep it in your backpack,” she had said. “Next time, we’ll plant it together. There’s a place for it beside the others.” Pip had promised to come before dark today. All the way to the river, he had been imagining where his flower might stand among hers.\n\nSelect up to 4,000 characters here with the mouse, or hold Shift while using the arrow keys. You can edit your full draft here, too. Both writing boxes show the same draft. Selecting words leaves your draft and previously chosen ending unchanged.",
